# Docs

Use this rule when editing managed docs. The `docs` skill owns setup, audit,
lifecycle, templates, references, and assets. Invoke that skill for any
non-trivial docs work.

## Bucket Profiles

- `services/<svc>/docs/` is a **service bucket**.
- `docs/` at repo root, or a domain repo `docs/`, is a **library bucket**.
- Service bucket required files: `README.md`, `PASSPORT.md`, `spec.md`,
  `backlog.md`.
- Library buckets must not contain `PASSPORT.md`, `spec.md`, or `backlog.md`.
- Both profiles use `adr/`, `proposals/`, `guides/`, `reference/`,
  `incidents/`, and `archive/{proposals,guides,reference}/`.
- Buckets may add indexed category folders, such as
  `docs/infrastructure/nats/`, when a domain has enough docs to justify its
  own local index.

## Markdown Header

Every managed Markdown doc starts with:

```markdown
<!-- doc-meta -->
> **Status:** draft | active | accepted | rejected | implemented | superseded | archived
> **Type:** overview | passport | roadmap | spec | backlog | proposal | adr | guide | reference | incident
> **Owner:** <gitlab handle or team>
> **Updated:** YYYY-MM-DD
```

JSON sidecars, including `reference/service.catalog.json`, do not carry
doc-meta.

## Type Boundaries

- `PASSPORT.md`: Markdown-first service entrypoint. No YAML frontmatter.
- `reference/service.catalog.json`: machine-readable service facts.
- `proposals/`: options under review; status becomes `accepted`,
  `rejected`, `implemented`, or `archived`. Do not use `decided` as status.
- `adr/`: durable accepted decisions, `NNN-slug.md`; body immutable after
  acceptance.
- `guides/`: living how-to/runbook content. Guides explain how; ADRs explain
  why.
- `reference/`: factual contracts/schemas/env/API docs tied to source files.
- `incidents/`: append-only postmortems, `YYYY-MM-DD-slug.md`.
- `spec.md`: in-flight acceptance criteria.
- `backlog.md`: future/deferred work.
- `ROADMAP.md`: short priority ordering with links.
- Category folders: local grouping only. They do not change doc-meta,
  lifecycle, or type semantics.

## Promotion Heuristics

- A guide with alternatives, trade-offs, or "we decided" should usually
  become an ADR plus a smaller guide if steps remain.
- An accepted proposal may produce an ADR, but only when the decision should
  be durable architectural/operational memory.
- A rejected proposal remains a proposal with `Status: rejected`; it does not
  need an ADR unless the rejection itself is an important policy.
- A shipped proposal can become `Status: implemented`.
- A reference containing opinions should split into reference facts plus a
  proposal or ADR.

## Required Section Shapes

For complete templates and validation checklists, the `docs` skill loads:

`plugins/umo-sdlc/skills/docs/references/docs-shape.md`

Minimum required sections:

| Type | Required sections |
|------|-------------------|
| overview | `#`, `## Quick links` |
| passport | `## Purpose`, `## Service Identity`, `## What It Provides`, `## What It Depends On`, `## How To Work On It`, `## Agent Read-Next`, `## Sharp Edges`, `## Operational Notes`, `## See Also` |
| proposal | `## Summary`, `## Problem`, `## Goals`, `## Non-goals`, `## Options Considered`, `## Decision`, `## Risks`, `## Success Criteria` |
| adr | `## Context`, `## Decision`, `## Consequences`, `## Alternatives Considered` |
| guide | `## When to use`, `## Prerequisites`, `## Steps`, `## Rollback / Safety Net`, `## Related` |
| reference | `## Source`, `## Contract`, `## Examples`, `## Related` |
| incident | `## Timeline`, `## Impact`, `## Root Cause`, `## Detection`, `## Mitigation`, `## Lessons`, `## Follow-ups` |
| spec | `## Acceptance criteria` |
| backlog | `## Up next`, `## Later`, `## Considered, not doing` |
| roadmap | `## In flight`, `## Up next`, `## After that` |

## Forbidden

- Adding YAML frontmatter to `PASSPORT.md`.
- Creating managed Markdown without doc-meta.
- Putting ADR content in `guides/`.
- Putting mutable runbook steps in ADRs.
- Editing accepted ADR bodies.
- Deleting completed spec criteria.
- Updating passport facts without updating `reference/service.catalog.json`
  when the sidecar exists.
- Creating category folders without a `README.md` index and root bucket link.
